import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { ToastProvider, ToastViewport, Toast, ToastAction } from '../../../../packages/platform/atoms/src/components/ui/toast';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    className: {
      type: "string",
      value: "custom-class",
      label: "Class Name",
    },
    children: {
      type: "string",
      value: "Action",
      label: "Button Text",
    },
  });

  return (
    <ToastProvider swipeDirection="right">
      <div className="relative">
        <Toast
          open={true}
          onOpenChange={() => {}}
          duration={Infinity}
        >
          <div className="flex gap-2">
            <div>Toast Message</div>
            <ToastAction
              altText="Action button"
              className={state.className.value}
              onClick={() => console.log("ToastAction clicked")}
            >
              {state.children.value}
            </ToastAction>
          </div>
        </Toast>
        <ToastViewport />
      </div>
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes to fix the error:

1. Added required props to `ToastProvider`:
   - `swipeDirection="right"` to specify the swipe direction

2. Added required props to `Toast` component:
   - `open={true}` to make the toast visible
   - `onOpenChange` handler
   - `duration={Infinity}` to keep the toast visible for the preview

3. Added required props to `ToastAction`:
   - `altText` prop which is required for accessibility

4. Wrapped the content in a proper structure:
   - Added a container div with relative positioning
   - Added a flex container for proper layout
   - Added some sample toast content for context

5. Kept the existing state management and className handling

These changes should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')" error by providing all the required props and proper structure that the Radix UI Toast components expect.

The error was occurring because the Toast components were missing some required props and context that Radix UI needs for proper functioning. The Toast system is now properly configured with all necessary props and structure.

